### Q1. Which option, and why? (Plus missing option E and systemic scope from W)

* **Choice under current rules: Modified Option A (`REOPEN` to `held`)** (`B:39-41`)[cite: 1]. The owner's 2026-10-17 directive requires two things jointly: (1) *"Fable's stage is recorded as a HELD marker carrying its question (`[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` plus a `hold_question`) and is answered when the seat comes back"* (`B:9-11`), and (2) *"record a wall as a SEAT FAILURE, never as agreement"* (`B:11-12`)[cite: 1]. Meanwhile, `check_stage_panels.py` (`H:13-15, 39-41`) unconditionally raises `CLOSED-WHILE-HELD` if any stage in `STAGES = ("assess", "research", "review")` (`B:25`) has a non-empty `live_holds()` on a row with `row.get("state") == "closed"`[cite: 1, 2]. Options B and C (`B:42-45`) violate `B:10` by substituting `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` for `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` on the walled `research`/`review` stage (leaving `live_holds()` empty in `H:26` so the stage reads `ok 9/9` on stale answers, `B:31-32`)[cite: 1, 2]. Option D (`B:46`) leaves the walls counted as `is_answer() == True` (`T:17`), violating `B:11-12`[cite: 1, 2].
* **Reading of *"do not block a ruling or a commit on Fable"* and the missing Option E (`B:37, 50-51`):** Under Option A, neither the panel's **ruling** (by Astra + Grok + GLM 5.3, `B:9`) nor the code/ledger **commit** is blocked: the code fix and ruling commit normally while the ledger row's state is `held` (or `in work`, `B:32-33`, `H:16-18, 42-47`) awaiting Fable[cite: 1, 2]. However, if the owner intended *"do not block a ruling or a commit"* (`B:9`) to also mean *"do not block row closure (`state: closed`) when Astra + Grok + GLM 5.3 have approved closure"*, the brief's option list (`B:37-46`) lacks **Option E (`KEEP CLOSED, EXEMPT FABLE5 HOLDS IN H`)**: prefix `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` to the walled stage entries and extend `hold_question` (obeying `B:9-12`), keep the 9 rows `closed`, and amend `H:13-15, 39-41` so a `closed` row whose only `live` holds are `fable5` appends to `held` instead of `CLOSED-WHILE-HELD` `violations` (matching how `regress` holds already sit on `closed` rows, `B:20-21, 28`)[cite: 1, 2].
* **Closure objects under Option A (`B:40-41`):** Whether `check_stage_panels.py` (outside `H:1-47`) rejects a `closure` object on a non-`closed` row is **UNSETTLED** (settled by full `tools/pipeline/check_stage_panels.py`), though Astra's confirm on `ip30abortkill` explicitly ordered *"omit the closure object"* (`B:32-33`) so preserving the drafted closure text in the state note or hold note is the safe path[cite: 1, 2].
* **Angle 1 �?" Systemic scope (`W:1-36`) and structural check (`T:13-17`):**
  * **Scope:** Keep this fix scoped to the 16 post-2026-10-17 `fable5` entries in `C:6-55` plus `cxlaunchquotation` `[8]` (`2026-10-16`, `C:43`, an identical untokened `STALLED` `SEAT FAILURE` in the same review chain), and file the wider historical class (`497` entries across all `9` seats on `129` rows, `81` closed, from `2026-08` onward, `W:6-8`) as a separate row[cite: 1, 2]. `W:1, 3` warns that the keyword net is a correlate with known false positives (e.g., actual findings matching keywords in `W:19, 32, 33`), and many August/September entries (`W:11-28, 35`) were deliberate non-firings under earlier directives where `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` or stage exemption�?"not `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: ...]`�?"applies, or already-answered `"DEFANGED"` holds (`W:29-30`)[cite: 2].
  * **Structural check (not prose):** The root bug is `T:13-17`, where `is_answer(e)` defaults to `return True` (`T:17`) for every untokened entry[cite: 2]. To prevent any new untokened non-answer from being written: (1) add a structural check in `stage_tokens.py` / `check_stage_panels.py` that rejects (as a precommit violation) any entry where `is_answer(e)` is `True` (`T:13-17`) and `_note(e)`'s opening prefix matches the failure/non-firing markers (`NOT FIRED`, `SEAT FAILURE`, `walled`, `STALLED`, `not tried`, `HTTP 429`, `HTTP 529`, `usage limit`, `quota`, `403`, `DID NOT ANSWER`, `no answer`, `W:3-4`, `C:3`), or require an explicit positive answer token on all new answer entries so `T:17` never defaults untokened failure prose to `True`; and (2) make the panel-runner/ledger-writer automatically prepend `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: <seat>]` or `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` when recording a transport error/skip[cite: 1, 2].

### Q2. `cxlaunchquotation`, `dashokclass`, and `sgirekills` �?" held or discharged? (Angle 2: `T`'s `live_holds` vs `C`)

* **Angle 2 �?" Exact trace of `T:19-42` (`live_holds`) against `C:38-53` (`cxlaunchquotation` and `dashokclass`):**
