### Q3. The conversion's form (`B:56-58`)

* **Prefix the token in place to the existing entry (one entry, provenance kept)** (`B:56`, `T:1-2, 13-17, 28, 38-39`)[cite: 1, 2].
  * `is_held(e)` tests `HELD in _note(e)` (`T:2`) and `is_answer(e)` returns `False` when `HELD in n or NOTSEAT in n` (`T:15-16`), so prefixing `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` directly to the existing entry simultaneously stops it from counting as an answer and registers the hold while preserving its original `date` (`hd` at `T:28`) and index[cite: 2].
  * Adding a new `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` entry today (`2026-10-18`) beside a re-tagged `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` entry would set `hd = "2026-10-18"` (`T:28`) on `2026-10-17` walls (`sgirekills` `[45]`, `[49]`, `cxlaunchquotation` `[12]`, `[26]`, `[30]`, `dashokclass` `[29]`, `C:14-15, 39-41, 47`), falsifying when the hold began and blocking any `2026-10-18` answer from discharging it under `(e.get("date") or "") > hd` (`T:39`)[cite: 1, 2].
  * Where multiple walled entries exist in the same `(row, phase)` because later passes ran (`wiringcliff` `[28]`/`[32]` already followed by `[41]`/`[48]` in `C:7-8, 11-12`; `sgirekills` `[49]` followed by `[56]` in `C:15-16`; `sgirandomcolour` `[28]` followed by `[32]` in `C:20-21`; `cxlaunchquotation` `[8]`/`[12]`/`[26]` followed by `[30]` in `C:39-41, 43`), either mark the superseded earlier pass attempts `[NOT A SEAT ANSWER]` and the latest pass `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]`, or fix `T:38-39` to compare `(e_date, e_idx) > (hd, h_idx)` so a single later answer discharges all prior holds in that stage regardless of whether they share a calendar date[cite: 1, 2].

### Q4. Is this an OWNER decision, and what is the single question? (`B:59-60`)

* Under the literal text of `B:9-12` and `H:13-15, 39-41` (and Astra's `ip30abortkill` confirm in `B:30-34`), reopening the nine rows to `held` (Option A) is already required by existing rules; however, deciding whether *"do not block a ruling or a commit on Fable"* (`B:9`) was meant to also permit row **closure** (`state: closed`) while a `fable5` stage hold remains live (Option E vs Option A) is an **owner policy decision**[cite: 1, 2].
* **Single question for the owner:**
  > *"When Astra + Grok + GLM 5.3 approve closing a row but Fable walled on `research` or `review` (`[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]`), must the row stay `state: held` until Fable answers (reopening the 9 rows closed since 2026-10-17), or should `check_stage_panels.py` section H allow `state: closed` with a live `fable5` stage hold just as it already allows `closed` with a `regress` hold?"* (`B:9-12, 20-21, 25-28, 39-41`, `H:13-15, 39-41`)[cite: 1, 2].

### Q5. Which of B's premises is wrong? (`B:61-62`)

1. **Census completeness (`B:14-18, 61` vs `C:2, 43`, `W:1-36`):** Incomplete. On `cxlaunchquotation` itself, entry `[8]` (`2026-10-16`, `C:43`) is an untokened `SEAT FAILURE` (`STALLED`) with `answer=True held=False` missed only because `C:2` filtered for `>= 2026-10-17`[cite: 1]. Across the ledger, `W:6-8` shows `497` untokened keyword-matched entries (`75` for `fable5`, including `59` before `2026-10-17`, `W:6, 10, 36`) across `129` rows (`81` closed)[cite: 2]. Whether additional post-2026-10-17 non-answers exist outside `C:2-3`'s 400-character keyword list is **UNSETTLED** without the working-tree ledger file[cite: 1].
2. **Later Fable answer discharging any of the nine closed rows (`B:61-62` vs `C:13-53`, `T:28, 38-39`):** None of the nine closed rows has a later Fable answer that discharges its stage[cite: 1, 2]. The only row among the nine where Fable answered after an included wall is `cxlaunchquotation`, where V4 (`[18]`, `2026-10-17`, `C:44`) and V5 (`[22]`, `2026-10-17`, `C:45`) came after V3 (`[12]`, `2026-10-17`, `C:39`), and those neither discharge V3 in `live_holds()` (because `"2026-10-17" > "2026-10-17"` is `False` at `T:39`) nor discharge the later walls on V6 (`[26]`, `C:40`) and V7 (`[30]`, `C:41`)[cite: 1, 2].
3. **`cxlaunchquotation` pass history (`B:52` vs `C:39-45`):** Fable did not answer V3-V6 and wall only on V7; it stalled on v2 (`[8]`, `C:43`) and V3 (`[12]`, `C:39`) and walled on V6 (`[26]`, `C:40`) as well as V7 (`[30]`, `C:41`)[cite: 1].
4. **`live_holds()` discharge rule description (`B:26, 57-58` vs `T:28, 38-39`):** `live_holds()` checks strictly later calendar `date` (`>`), not later entry order in the phase, so same-day recovery answers fail to discharge same-day holds (`T:39`)[cite: 1, 2].
5. **`wiringcliff` stage & hold status (`B:20-21, 25-28` vs `C:6-12`):** `wiringcliff` `[28]` is in `design` (not in `STAGES`, `B:25`, `C:7`), and `wiringcliff` already has `[HELD AWAITING SEAT: fable5]` on later entries `[41]` (`design`, `C:11`) and `[48]` (`review`, `C:12`)[cite: 1].
6. **`ip30abortkill` state discrepancy (`B:32-33`):** `B:32-33` quotes Astra's confirm requiring `state: in work` and then states the row was committed `held`[cite: 1].

