26294:   "state_note": "*** A SEAT SAYS THE LADDER GAP MAY BE NARROWER THAN THIS ROW ASSUMES. 2026-08-27. ***\n\nReviewing `wdcoddstep`, the Fable seat noted that a **rung-3 cold-debugger probe looks\nBUILDABLE** for that defect -- real guest stores of 0xA0 plus a CDB, then real 4-byte\ndata-port loads through decode, on an in-tree wdc machine.  If so, that defect need not\nshelter under this row at all.\n\n**Which sharpens the owner question rather than answering it:** is the gap a genuine\nladder hole, or a habit of reaching for the offline differential because it is one second\ninstead of one boot?  *Three rounds shipped rung-1; nobody asked whether a rung-3 witness\nwas AVAILABLE for any of them.*  Worth one attempt before proposing a new term.\n\n*** A POLICY GAP THAT THREE ROUNDS HAVE NOW HIT INDEPENDENTLY.  Filed 2026-08-27. ***\n\n`b115` (#472), `wdcringambig`/`wdcrearmzero` (#473) and `fbclearread` (#474) all shipped a\nREAL FIX whose only evidence is a rung-1 offline differential plus a measured kill table.  The\nwitness ladder classes a rung-1 direct-call harness as a DETECTOR and never as a reproduction,\nso none of the five witness terms fits:\n\n* `boot:` / `probe:` / `construction:` -- false, and `probe:` is actively dangerous because\n  `check_witness.py`'s SHAPE regex would score it rung-3.  Its own header calls naming an\n  #include/direct-call harness there \"the laundering this field exists to make visible\".\n* `harness:` -- admitted ONLY when the round's SUBJECT is the test apparatus.  None of the\n  three qualifies; all three fix emulator code.\n* `none` -- defined by `state_semantics` as DOCUMENTED-ONLY, so on a round that shipped a fix\n  it asserts that no code changed.  **A wrong record, not a conservative one.**\n\nSo every such round parks at `held` carrying a prose note, and the note is doing the work a\nschema value should do.  That is survivable once; at three it is a pattern, and a fourth will\ncopy whichever note it happens to find.\n\n**THE QUESTION FOR THE OWNER:** does a fix shipped on rung-1 evidence alone need an explicit\nOWNER EXEMPTION per round, or should the ladder gain a term for it?  A candidate term is\n`detector:<path>` -- honest about what exists, structurally distinct from `probe:`, and it\nwould let `check_witness.py` tell \"fixed with a detector\" from \"documented only\", which it\ncannot do today.\n\n**NOT proposing the term unilaterally.**  Adding a ladder rung changes what every future round\nmay claim, and the ladder's existing terms were adjudicated rather than invented.  Work\ncontinues meanwhile: the three rows are `held` with honest notes, which is correct under the\ncurrent schema and costs nothing to revisit.\n",
