the unmapped-read scenario never share an emulator instance**, so bit 8 is clear whenever TEX is
read.  *"M10 establishes detection of a width-bit collision, not every existing-bit collision"* --
which is exactly the over-generalisation my CHANNEL table had made in a parenthesis.

